jcode (MIT)
===========
The Codemode sandbox tool (src/codemode/) is adapted from jcode, an open-source
Rust coding agent by Jeremy Huang (https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode),
distributed under the MIT License below. The QuickJS sandbox contract, the
script prelude, the tool-discovery surface (listTools / describeTool / the in
operator on tools), the session store and the risk-gated host are ported from
ref/codemode/{engine,lib,tests}.rs onto Loam's own policy and tool-registry
modules; the sandbox runtime itself is quickjs-emscripten, not jcode's code.

The cross-session file-touch notification feature in src/tools/fileTouch.ts,
src/tools/readState.ts, src/agent/reminders.ts and src/agent/loop.ts was
adapted from jcode (https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode), Copyright (c) 2025
Jeremy Huang, and is distributed under the MIT License below. The port was
re-implemented in TypeScript for Loam; the idea and the notice semantics (a
session is told when another session writes a file it already read, with a
short line-diff summary) come from jcode.

The Loam benchmark harness under bench/ and the local memory-budget primitives
under src/memory/ are adapted from jcode, a Rust coding agent
(https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode). Copyright (c) 2025 Jeremy Huang. MIT License.

  bench/fakeModel.ts    — ref/fake_model.py
  bench/rssSampler.ts   — ref/bench_memory_cli.py
  bench/memBench.ts     — ref/jcode_daemon_bench.py
  bench/appRamBench.ts  — ref/bench_memory_cli.py

The prompt-cache (KV) miss detection ported in `src/agent/kvCacheMonitor.ts`
adapts jcode's daemon-side `src/kv_cache_monitor.rs` design (provider usage
normalization, reusable-token boundary, miss-reason classification and the
human-readable summaries).

The TypeScript files under `bench/` were adapted from jcode, a coding agent
copyright (c) 2025 Jeremy Huang. Only bench/fakeModel.ts, bench/rssSampler.ts
and bench/memBench.ts are adapted from jcode; the rest of the app is original
Loam code.

